<body>

<h1>🚀 Diamond Tenant Copilot Studio: DEV → TEST → PROD Learning Journey</h1>

<div class="objective">
<h3>Learning Objective</h3>
<p>
Build a Copilot Studio agent in DEV, package it using Power Platform Solutions,
promote it through TEST, and deploy it to Microsoft Teams and Microsoft 365 Copilot,
following the same lifecycle discussed in the blog.
</p>
</div>

<h2>Phase 0 - Prepare Diamond Tenant</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">
<b>Claim your Diamond Tenant</b>

<ul>
<li>Open MDX</li>
<li>Claim Diamond Tenant</li>
<li>Launch tenant</li>
<li>Verify Copilot Studio opens</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">
<b>Attach Azure Subscription</b>

<ul>
<li>Request BYOT Azure subscription</li>
<li>Associate with Diamond Tenant</li>
<li>Deploy Agent 365 Add-On</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="warning">
Do NOT change tenant passwords.
The Diamond documentation explicitly warns this may break provisioning and add-on experiences.
</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 1 - Build the Environment Strategy</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">
<b>Create DEV Environment</b>

<p>Name: Zava-Agent-DEV</p>

<p>Purpose:</p>
<ul>
<li>Agent building</li>
<li>Prompt engineering</li>
<li>Connector testing</li>
<li>Topic design</li>
<li>Power Automate integration</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">
<b>Create TEST Environment</b>

<p>Name: Zava-Agent-UAT</p>

<ul>
<li>Solution import testing</li>
<li>Persona validation</li>
<li>Business acceptance testing</li>
<li>Teams deployment testing</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">
<b>Create PROD Environment</b>

<p>Name: Zava-Agent-PROD</p>

<ul>
<li>Published agent</li>
<li>Business consumption</li>
<li>Teams deployment</li>
<li>M365 Copilot deployment</li>
</ul>
</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 2 - Choose a Diamond Tenant Persona</h2>

<div class="step">

Pick a realistic business owner:

<ul>
<li>Security Operations - Isaac Fielder</li>
<li>Enterprise IT Architect - Lydia Bauer</li>
<li>App Developer - Sarah Perez</li>
<li>Chief Marketing Officer - Cecil Folk</li>
<li>Sales - Mona Kane</li>
<li>Factory Operations - Karin Blair</li>
</ul>

Your first agent should have a business sponsor.
</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 3 - Create the DEV Agent</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">
<b>Open Copilot Studio</b>

<ul>
<li>Switch to DEV environment</li>
<li>Create a new agent</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

<b>Create Agent: Zava Marketing Advisor</b>

Instructions:

<ul>
<li>Add description</li>
<li>Add starter instructions</li>
<li>Enable Generative Answers</li>
<li>Enable Microsoft knowledge grounding</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

<b>Add Knowledge Sources</b>

Use Zava content contained in Diamond Tenant:

<ul>
<li>Campaigns</li>
<li>Campaign Messaging</li>
<li>Brand and Design</li>
<li>Go To Market</li>
<li>Products</li>
</ul>

</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 4 - Add Actions</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Create Power Automate flows:

<ul>
<li>Submit marketing request</li>
<li>Create task</li>
<li>Send approval</li>
<li>Escalate issue</li>
</ul>

Expose each flow as an Action.
</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 5 - Solution Packaging (Most Important Lesson)</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Create Managed Solution

<p>Name:</p>

<code>ZavaMarketingAgentSolution</code>

Include:

<ul>
<li>Agent</li>
<li>Prompts</li>
<li>Connector references</li>
<li>Flows</li>
<li>Environment variables</li>
</ul>

</div>

<div class="check">

✅ This is the biggest concept in the DEV → PROD blog.

Never move agents manually.

Move solutions.

</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 6 - Deploy to TEST</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Export Solution from DEV

<ul>
<li>Managed</li>
<li>Version 1.0.0</li>
</ul>

</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Import into TEST Environment

Validate:

<ul>
<li>Agent functions</li>
<li>Knowledge works</li>
<li>Flows execute</li>
<li>Authentication works</li>
</ul>

</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 7 - Teams Publishing</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

From TEST:

<ul>
<li>Open Channels</li>
<li>Microsoft Teams</li>
<li>Publish</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Install into Teams

Validate:

<ul>
<li>Chat experience</li>
<li>Adaptive cards</li>
<li>Actions</li>
<li>Permissions</li>
</ul>

</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 8 - M365 Copilot Deployment</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Configure Microsoft 365 Copilot channel

Validate:

<ul>
<li>Agent appears in Copilot</li>
<li>M365 content grounding works</li>
<li>Search experiences work</li>
<li>Agent instructions execute correctly</li>
</ul>
</div>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 9 - Governance</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Review:

<ul>
<li>DLP Policies</li>
<li>Copilot Policies</li>
<li>Sensitivity Labels</li>
<li>Purview Controls</li>
</ul>
</div>

<p>
The Diamond Tenant includes Purview governance,
DLP policies,
Copilot controls,
Communication Compliance,
retention labels,
and sensitivity labels specifically for demonstrating governance and AI protection scenarios.
</p>

<hr>

<h2>Phase 10 - Production Promotion</h2>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Export Solution v1.0.0 from TEST
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Import Managed Solution into PROD
</div>

<div class="step">
<input type="checkbox">

Publish to:
<ul>
<li>Teams</li>
<li>Microsoft 365 Copilot</li>
</ul>
</div>

<hr>

<h2>Capstone Challenge</h2>

<p><b>Build ALL FOUR:</b></p>

<ol>
<li>HR Policy Agent</li>
<li>Marketing Advisor Agent</li>
<li>Sales Briefing Agent</li>
<li>Security Triage Agent</li>
</ol>

<p>
When you complete these four and move each through DEV→TEST→PROD using Solutions,
you will have learned the same lifecycle used by enterprise Copilot Studio teams.
</p>

</body>
</html>